Lua 5.4.9, from https://www.lua.org/ftp/lua-5.4.9.tar.gz (the library files in src/, without lua.c, luac.c
and the Makefile). The files here are unchanged, so they can be replaced with a newer release as-is. The sandbox
(which libraries are opened, no file access, text chunks only, capped string.rep and table.move/insert/remove/sort, and the work budget) lives
in ../scripting/LuaEngine.cpp.

One file is patched: patched/lstrlib.c is a copy of lstrlib.c that is built instead of it. It charges the work
done by pattern matching and plain searches (match steps, class bytes scanned, candidate positions) to the
running script's work budget through melonade_charge_work() (MELONADE_CHARGE), which raises an error once the
budget is gone, so that big searches and backtracking patterns can't hang the emulator thread. lmemfind() also
takes the lua_State for that. Every change is marked "melonade". When upgrading Lua, copy the new lstrlib.c into
patched/ and redo those changes.
